" :db/id 17592186070077} {:answer/id #uuid "1cacef46-ef5e-5b1b-814c-14b3f44ea4fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a =-2, b = 2" :db/id 17592186070078}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3f914bec-7e6e-58f8-a49c-484a6a89ef3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186070073}] :question/id #uuid "90bf8b55-699c-5e18-b484-90473cb6a72f" :question/math-academy-id "q-12457" :question/problem "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n\n${-7a + 2b = 18; -6a + 6b = 0$"} {:db/id 17592186074047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "108d90bc-6b5c-5888-a441-c0910faf7b57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186070290} {:answer/id #uuid "3afa1d5f-dfe6-59bc-8683-638f0716320d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id 17592186070291} {:answer/id #uuid "5b963b53-bada-5f5f-9e14-bb49282b0719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id 17592186070292} {:answer/id #uuid "637fb8f3-b4ed-5b3b-b5dc-ae08c01f9ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id 17592186070293} {:answer/id #uuid "71ce6b5e-047a-5e92-8750-073b719123cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id 17592186070294}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8b1211a7-7190-520c-ac4c-581ede5f3f0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186070289}] :question/id #uuid "a7c18dc6-0363-5db7-9c51-22de1db359fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-18483" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n${5q + 55 = 0; 2p + 3q + 3 = 0$"} {:db/id 17592186496252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ed3f880-96ed-5fd6-824f-be81fbff3e25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186495753} {:answer/id #uuid "92cf3e39-98db-564f-a3c5-ad104dff9377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id 17592186495833} {:answer/id #uuid "adefce60-eb41-5a32-906f-e3cd671a3daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id 17592186495899} {:answer/id #uuid "b6612f39-f352-56c1-817b-399df43c996f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186495919} {:answer/id #uuid "e81c2d81-0ae0-51a8-90a5-645bcd295610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id 17592186496022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ed3f880-96ed-5fd6-824f-be81fbff3e25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186495753} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca46e4e1-5150-5d40-98c3-33efe3175aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186496180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "498d2b3f-6756-59df-bd3d-256bb722b0aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-112214" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $y-x?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y=0 \\\\ 5y-15x+10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y=0 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 5y-15x+10=0 & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2),$ we can isolate $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-15x+10 & =0 \\\\ 5y & =15x-10 \\\\ y & =3x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $3x-2$  into equation $(1)$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21x-9y & =0 \\\\ 21x-9(3x-2) & =0 \\\\ 21x-27x+18 & =0 \\\\ -6x+18 & =0 \\\\ 18 & =6x \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=3$ into $y=3x-2,$ then we can find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-2 \\\\ y & =3(3)-2 \\\\ y & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3,\\,y=7.$ So,\n\n$$\ny-x=7-3=4.\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186496314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff409c69-65be-5db8-9082-449cc256ae35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186496070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff409c69-65be-5db8-9082-449cc256ae35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186496070} :answer-field/id #uuid "d502feb6-12a4-5b5d-a239-789af82850e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186496187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be1f5640-6243-5fce-a7c7-5b82c5d69ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186495929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be1f5640-6243-5fce-a7c7-5b82c5d69ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186495929} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef8a675b-4a10-5910-adfc-f84ccbe5facf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186496207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d389f84f-6df2-5d57-9702-acb625d9c80f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181207" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q=-18 \\\\ 4p+3q+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(p,q)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(p,q)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q=-18 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 4p+3q+2=0 & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(1),$ we can solve for $p$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-6q & =-18 \\\\ 3p & =6q-18 \\\\ p & =2q-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=2q-6$ into equation $(2)$ and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2q-6)+3q+2 & =0 \\\\ 8q-24+3q+2 & =0 \\\\ 11q & =22 \\\\ q & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $q=2$ into equation $(1),$ then we can find the value of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-6(2) & =-18 \\\\ 3p-12 & =-18 \\\\ 3p & =-6 \\\\ p & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-2,\\,q=2,$ which can be expressed as $(-2,2).$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}
